# zentone SIMD tier isolation — BENCH ADDED BUT NOT RUN (crate does not build here)
date: 2026-07-28
host: Apple M4 Pro (12 core), macOS, aarch64

## Status: NO MEASUREMENT

benches/tier_isolation.rs was added for parity with the other zen crates
(garb / linear-srgb / zenwebp / butteraugli / zenresize / fast-ssim2 / zensim /
zenblend / heic / zenjpeg all got the same bench). It has NOT been run, because
zentone does not build on this machine at all:

  error: failed to get `polyfit` as a dependency of package `zentone v0.2.0`
  Caused by: unable to update /Users/lilith/work/polyfit

`Cargo.toml:81` declares `polyfit = { path = "../../polyfit" }`, and that
sibling is not present here. This is PRE-EXISTING and unrelated to the bench:
`cargo check` fails identically with the Cargo.toml change stashed. It is a hard
dependency (not optional, not feature-gated), so no target in this crate can be
built or benchmarked without that sibling checked out.

So: NO NEON-vs-scalar numbers are claimed for zentone. The bench is committed
so it runs for free on a machine that has the sibling; it follows the same
verified pattern as the other ten, but it is unverified here and is labelled as
such rather than being presented as coverage.

## Note on the dependency itself

A mandatory `path = "../../polyfit"` dependency means the crate is unbuildable
from a bare checkout — CI, a fresh clone, or any machine without that exact
sibling layout. That is the same class of problem the zen workspace already
warns about for committed scripts ("NEVER hardcode a sibling-worktree path").
Worth either publishing polyfit, vendoring it, or making it optional. Not
changed here — altering a crate's dependency wiring is well outside a
NEON-optimisation pass, and doing it blind on a machine that cannot build the
result would be worse than leaving it.
